 array['International event announced for Egypt', 'Festival / race / conference with international attendance', 'Sponsor programme announced'],
 array['International guests arrive with high expectations and no local contacts', 'Organiser team is stretched on event operations, not guest requests', 'Hotels, transfers and dinners booked piecemeal by guests, with no quality control'],
 'One accountable NOYA desk (named lead + 24/7 line) that handles guest arrivals, transport, accommodation, dining and last-minute problems, reporting to the organiser.',
 array['24/7 guest line', 'Airport meet & greet and VIP handling', 'Chauffeured transfers', 'Accommodation sourcing and room blocks', 'Restaurant and nightlife access', 'Pre/post-event experiences', 'On-site concierge desk'],
 array['Egypt ground team with hotel, transport and venue partners', 'Single point of contact for the organiser', 'Rates negotiated through NOYA partners'],
 array['HOTEL', 'TRANSPORT', 'SECURITY', 'RESTAURANT', 'EXPERIENCE'],
 array['Your international guests need a local host you do not have to manage', 'Protect the guest experience outside the venue — the part your team cannot control'],
 $j${"subject": "{{event}} guests in {{destination}}", "body": "Hi {{first_name}},\n\n{{trigger_detail}} — congratulations. With international guests arriving for {{event}}, most of what they judge you on happens outside the venue: arrivals, transfers, where they stay, where they eat.\n\nNOYA runs that layer on the ground in Egypt — one desk, one named lead, a 24/7 line for your guests, and our hotel and transport partners behind it. {{proof}}\n\nWould a 15-minute call next week be useful to see whether a guest desk for {{event}} makes sense?\n\nAdam Elshazly\nFounder, NOYA Concierge"}$j$::jsonb,
 'Hi {{first_name}} — saw {{event}} is coming to {{destination}}. NOYA runs on-ground guest services in Egypt (arrivals, transport, hotels, dining, 24/7 line). Worth a quick chat about your international guests?',
 array['How many international guests, talent and sponsor guests do they expect?', 'Who handles guest requests today — in-house, agency, nobody?', 'Which hotels are they already using?', 'Where did guest experience go wrong at previous editions?', 'Decision timeline and budget owner'],
 $j$[{"objection": "Our agency already handles this.", "response": "Good — we work alongside agencies as their Egypt ground layer. Who at the agency owns the on-ground guest side?"}, {"objection": "Too early / too late.", "response": "Fair. What date would be right to talk guest services — can I put it in both our diaries?"}, {"objection": "Budget is committed.", "response": "Guest services can be paid per guest or by sponsors directly, not from the event budget. Worth a look?"}]$j$::jsonb,
 'Scope: guest profile and volumes · Desk model (on-site hours, 24/7 line) · Services menu with per-guest pricing · Partners and rates · Reporting to organiser · Commercial terms (per-guest fee or fixed desk fee + pass-through costs).',
 $j$[{"day": 3, "channel": "EMAIL", "purpose": "Add one concrete idea", "message": "One practical idea for {{event}}: a single WhatsApp line for all international guests, staffed by NOYA, so your team never fields a hotel or car request. Happy to show how it runs."}, {"day": 7, "channel": "LINKEDIN", "purpose": "Right person", "message": "Hi {{first_name}} — who on your team looks after international guest experience for {{event}}? Happy to take it to them directly."}, {"day": 14, "channel": "EMAIL", "purpose": "Close the loop", "message": "I will leave this here — if guest services for {{event}} become a need, NOYA can be set up within a week. Good luck with the edition."}]$j$::jsonb,
 array['Sponsor guest programme', 'Talent/artist concierge', 'Post-event Egypt extensions', 'Private dinners and after-parties'],
